<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>GERONA, Spain 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the second</p>
<p>round of the European championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona)</p>
<p>Turkey 81 Israel 71 (halftime 21-35)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Turkey - Orhun Ene 19, Ufuk Sarica 18, Tamer Oyguc 15,</p>
<p>Ibrahim Kutluay 13, Mirsad Turkcan 11.</p>
<p>Israel - Tomer Steinhauer 23, Oded Katash 17, Nadav Henefeld</p>
<p>19, Doron Sheffer 9.</p>
<p>Group F (in Badalona)</p>
<p>Yugoslavia 88 Germay 73 (47-30)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Yugoslavia - Zoran Savic 16, Aleksandar Djordjevic 14,</p>
<p>Zeljko Rebraca 12, Nikola Bulatovic 12, Dejan Tomasevic 11.</p>
<p>Germany - Sascha Hupmann 15, Vladimir Bogojeric 12, Ademola</p>
<p>Okulaja 10, Henrik Roedl 10, Henning Harnisch 9.</p>
<p>Places 13-16 (between teams eliminated at the end of the</p>
<p>first phase):</p>
<p>Latvia 76 Ukraine 84 (42-35)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Latvia - Ralfs Jansons 17, Ainars Bagatskis 15, Andrejs</p>
<p>Bondarenko 14, Roberts Stelmahers 11, Edgars Sneps 10</p>
