<p>Evgueni Murzine 14, Leonid Yailo 13, Grigory Khizhnyak 4, Vadim</p>
<p>Pudzrey 4.</p>
<p>Bosnia 61 Slovenia 73 (halftime 21-46)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Bosnia - Gordan Firic 12, Haris Mujeznovic 9, Aris Beciragic</p>
<p>9, Dzevad Alihodzic 8, Sajo Bukva 9.</p>
<p>Slovenia - Radosav Nesterovic 20, Ivica Jurkovic 17, Marko</p>
<p>Milic 13, Boris Gorenc 12, Jurij Zdovc 7.</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona)</p>
<p>Russia 93 France 80 (49-40)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Russia - Andrei Fetissov 17, Mikhail Mikhailov 16, Vassily</p>
<p>Karassev 11, Igor Koudelin 11, Evgueny Kissourin 9, Sergei</p>
<p>Babkov 9.</p>
<p>France - Cyril Julian 17, Thierry Gadou 14, Frederic</p>
<p>Fauthoux 11, Yann Bonato 11.</p>
<p>Group F (in Badalona)</p>
<p>Italy 63 Spain 60 (25-36)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Italy - Carlton Myers 20, Gegor Fucka 16, Denis Marconato 9.</p>
<p>Spain - Alberto Herreros 15, Rafael Jofresa 13, Roger</p>
<p>Esteller 12.</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona):</p>
<p>Greece 73 Lithuania 66 (halftime 34-18)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Greece: Demetrios Pananikolaou 15, Ioannis Giannoulis 11,</p>
<p>Agelos Koronios 11, George Sigalas 9, Nikos Ekonomou 9.</p>
<p>Lithuania: Saulius Stombergas 16, Gintaras Einkis 12, Darius</p>
<p>Lukminas 10, Arturas Karnisovas 9, Virginius Praskevicius 8.</p>
<p>Poland 77 Croatia 76 (halftime 38-50)  </p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Poland: Maciej Zielinski 16, Piotr Szybilski 12, Mariusz</p>
<p>Bacik 12, Andrezj Pluta 8, Adam Wojcik 8.</p>
<p>Croatia: Slaven Rimac 20, Sinisa Kelecevic 15, Niksa Prkacin</p>
<p>13, Damir Mulaomerovic 11, Emilio Kovacic 3.</p>
